                                Scratch, a play about nothing.

Benedick, exists.
Bianca, who has money.
Hecate, who helps print.

Shylock, a merchant who likes coin$.
Puck, a fairy who likes to stop the action periodically.
Othello, a general in search of a New Line.
Macduff, 100.

                                Act I: Hello.
                                Scene I: Hello.
[Enter Hecate]

[Enter Shylock]
Hecate: Thou art the cube of a good horse.
        Thou art the product of thyself and a good old horse.
        Thou art the sum of thyself and a good old horse.
[Exit Shylock]

[Enter Puck]
Hecate: Thou art the sum of a horse and a good horse.
        Thou art the product of thyself and a good old good old horse.
        Thou art the difference between thyself and a good horse.
[Exit Puck]

[Enter Othello]
Hecate: Thou art the difference between Puck and Shylock!
[Exit Othello]

[Enter Bianca]
Hecate: Thou art a beautiful embroidered fair fine lovely sweet pretty charming blossoming angel.
        Thou art the difference between thyself and Othello. Thou art the difference between thyself and a red rose.
[Exit Bianca]

[Enter Macduff]
Hecate: Thou art the square of Othello.
[Exit Macduff]

[Enter Benedick]
Hecate: Thou art as stuffed as Shylock. Speak thy mind!
        Thou art the quotient between Bianca and Macduff. Open thy heart!
        Thou art as stuffed as Puck. Speak thy mind!
        Thou art the remainder of the quotient between Bianca and Macduff.
        Art thou more misused than Othello? If so, thou art nothing.
        Art thou as small as nothing? If so, open thy heart!
        Thou art the remainder of the quotient between Bianca and Macduff. Open thy heart!
        Thou art as lying as Othello. Speak thy mind!

[Exit Benedick]
[Exit Hecate]